ROOT CAUSE (exact, reproduced):
  .gitattributes sets '* -text' (byte-identical checkouts, see its header).
  '-text' makes git treat EVERY file as non-text, so 'git diff --numstat'
  reports '-' (binary, 0 lines) for all 678 corpus blobs in the diff.
  GitHub does NOT honour '-text' for additions accounting; it sniffs content
  for NUL bytes.  162 of the newly-added fuzz seed-corpus blobs contain NO
  NUL byte, so GitHub counts them as TEXT and charges their lines as additions.
  They are all ADDED files, which is why deletions are unaffected, and git
  already counts them as changed files, which is why the file count matches.

